cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Regional HIV Spatial Patterns Mapped Across Ghanaian District Boundaries: 261-District Analysis"
abstract: >
 Reproducible analysis pipeline for a spatial epidemiological study of HIV
 prevalence and its socioeconomic determinants across all 261 of Ghana's
 census districts (261 districts share 260 unique GSS 2023 boundary
 polygons). Methods include Global Moran's I, Bivariate LISA, Getis-Ord Gi*,
 spatial lag and spatial error regression (specification chosen via
 Lagrange multiplier diagnostics), geographically weighted regression
 (GWR), LASSO, and Random Forest with SHAP interpretability. Top predictor:
 VCT uptake (|SHAP|=0.639); Global Moran's I=0.920 (KNN k=4, p=0.001).
